
This tar files contains clang and other tools to compile libraries and binaries in Android

Also included are the files necessary to compile binaries and libraries for Andrroid on arm64 CPU from the Android NDKs r27d, r28b, and r29.

Note that tar files with the files from the older Android NDK versions can be found here:

http://bnsmb.de/files/public/Android/archive/ndk_for_clang19_toolchain/


Since version June 2026 this tar file also contains the toolchain with gcc 16.1.1 and the other necessary files to compile C/C++ source with gcc or g++.
Note: The gcc toolchain contains all necessary files to compile C and C++ programs with GCC - an Android NDK is not required for this toolchain.


There is also a GitHub repository with the files for the clang19 toolchain:

https://github.com/bnsmb/clang19_toolchain_for_android

This repository always contain the latest version of all files from this tar file.

Use the commnad

git clone https://github.com/bnsmb/clang19_toolchain_for_android

to download the latest version of the clang19 toolchain. 


To use the clang19 toolchain, these steps must be carried out:

unpack the tar file in 

/data/local/tmp

this creates the directories with the tools in the directory 

/data/local/tmp/sysroot


Then execute the script to configure the clang environment

/data/local/tmp/sysroot/create_clang_env.sh

The script create_clang_env.sh creates the necessary directories and files for the clang19 toolchain. The script also initializes the OpenSSH config files and creates the necessary ssh host keys to start the sshd on the phone. The script only needs to be executed once (but it can be executed more than once without problems).


To init the clang environment source the file

/data/local/tmp/sysroot/bin/init_clang19_env

This command must be executed once in each adb session if the clang19 toolchain is to be used.

Now you can use the clang to compile binaries or libraries for Android.


The tar file also contains some simple test programs to test the compiler. Use the command

/data/local/tmp/sysroot/compile_examples.sh

to compile the sample test programs.


Notes:

The default NDK version is stored in the variable NDK defined in the file init_clang19_env:

[clang19 toolchain] 127|ASUS_I006D:/data/local/tmp $ grep NDK= /data/local/tmp/sysroot/bin/init_clang19_env                                    
  NDK="${NDK:=r27d}"
[clang19 toolchain] ASUS_I006D:/data/local/tmp $ 

To use another Android NDK version included in the tar file either change the variable NDK in the file

/data/local/tmp/sysroot/bin/init_clang19_env

or set the variable NDK before sourcing the file /data/local/tmp/sysroot/bin/init_clang19_env :

NDK=<ndk_version> source /data/local/tmp/sysroot/bin/init_clang19_env 


The default pkg-config tool configured is pkg-config; to use pkgconf instead of pkg-config set the environment variable PKG_CONFIG 

PKG_CONFIG=/data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/clang19/bin/pkgconf


The include file sysroot/usr/include/add_missing_definitions.h contains definitions and functions required by various Unix tools but missing in Android.


Some configure scripts and makefiles for standard Unix tools use libraries that are not available (and not needed) in Android, e.g. libpthread.so.

A dummy (= empty) libpthread.so is part of the clang19 toolchain:

[clang19 toolchain] ASUS_I006D:/data/local/tmp/sysroot $ ls -l usr/lib/libpthread.*                                                                                                               
-rw-r--r-- 1 shell shell 1218 2025-09-21 15:04 usr/lib/libpthread.a
-rw-r--r-- 1 shell shell 5272 2025-09-21 15:04 usr/lib/libpthread.so
[clang19 toolchain] ASUS_I006D:/data/local/tmp/sysroot $ 


To create another dummy (empty) library to satisfy the requirements of these configure scripts or make files the script

create_dummy_lib.sh

can be used.


Example:

Create the dummy library libutil.so :


[clang19 toolchain] ASUS_I006D:/data/local/tmp/sysroot $ cd /data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/lib                                                                                                       
[clang19 toolchain] ASUS_I006D:/data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/lib $ 

[clang19 toolchain] ASUS_I006D:/data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/lib $ create_dummy_lib.sh util                                                                                                         
Creating the library "libutil" ....
-rw-rw-rw- 1 shell shell 1218 2025-12-21 17:47 libutil.a
-rwxrwxrwx 1 shell shell 5272 2025-12-21 17:47 libutil.so
[clang19 toolchain] ASUS_I006D:/data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/lib $ 



To init the environment only for gcc open an adb session and execute the command

source bin/init_gcc_env

Now you can use gcc and c++ to compile C and C++ source files.


Please note that the directory /data/local/tmp/sysroot is hardcoded in the binaries and scripts used for gcc.


