Notes

Some standard Android programs do not work very well with the new binaries in /data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/bin -- therefore it is recommended that
/system/bin/ is placed in the PATH variable before /data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/bin

The script init_clang19_env creates some aliase for the executables in the clang19 toolchain. The script also creates aliase for each file in /system_ext/bin and
in /product/bin that is also part of the clang19 toolchain.
The list of aliase created by the init script is stored in the environment variable NEW_ALIAS.

The script init_clang19_env also defines two functions to define or clear the aliase:

Use the function "clear_aliase" to undefine all aliase for the binaries from the clang19 toolchain; use the function "define_aliase" to (re)define the aliase
for the binaries from the clang19 toolchain. 

The test for the execution permissions like this

 [ -x /bin/sh ] && echo ok

does now work in the bash from this tar archive.

To install additional Perl Modules with cpan, use this syntax

PATH=/data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/bin:$PATH cpan

There are multiple versions of cmake in the tar file:

[clang19 toolchain] ASUS_I006D:/data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/bin $ ls -hl cmake*                                                                                                                                                                             
lrwxrwxrwx 1 shell shell  13 2026-03-18 20:30 cmake -> ./cmake-4.3.0
-rwxrwxr-x 1 shell shell 10M 2026-01-05 16:41 cmake-3.30
-rwxrwxr-x 1 shell shell 11M 2026-01-05 16:41 cmake-4.0.1
-rwxr-xr-x 1 shell shell 19M 2026-03-19 15:53 cmake-4.3.0
[clang19 toolchain] ASUS_I006D:/data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/bin $ 


To use another cmake version just modify the symbolic link for cmake.


